menu "Kid pager"

    config PAGER_MOVE_TRIALS
        bool "Server move: run trials, switch brokers and bearers, advertise mvc and brc"
        default n
        help
            With this option an order from a source server (cfg.mv) is stored and acked, replies wait while
            one is held, and the pager connects to the new broker (over the direct bearer, also from Soracom
            Beam), commits on a signed proof or reverts, runs the long-run reconnect schedule, and sends /status
            `mvc:1` so a relay will order a move at all. It also acts on cfg.br (try Beam again, fall back to
            direct without a proof) and sends `brc:1`.

            Without it the pager cannot finish a move, so it takes none on: an order is acked and refused
            (`fail`/`rej`), no pending identity is stored, and replies and cfg.ca are not held for it. An order
            an earlier image stored is reported `fail`/`rej` at boot and its pending identity is dropped. A
            `moving` receipt from a frozen source still holds replies for a day. cfg.br is left alone. Every
            image carries the KPCAPS1:mv; tag, which only says the image can read a committed slot.

            The broker switch within one power cycle is not verified on the modem (docs/MOVE_FIRMWARE_DESIGN.md
            §13.1). Leave this off until it is.

endmenu
